For $v\colon\mathbb{Z}/n\to\mathbb{C}$, write
  $e_i = \mathrm{segment}\,\mathbb{R}\,(v_i)\,(v_{i+1})$ for the closed edge
  segments. $\mathrm{IsSimplePolygon}\,v$ holds when
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item every edge is nondegenerate: $v_i \neq v_{i+1}$;
  \item consecutive edges meet only in the shared vertex:
        $e_i \cap e_{i+1} = \{v_{i+1}\}$;
  \item non-adjacent edges are disjoint: if $i \neq j$, $i+1 \neq j$ and
        $j+1 \neq i$ then $e_i \cap e_j = \emptyset$.
  \end{enumerate}
